{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שמור ושמעת", :translit "shmor v'shamata", :gloss "Observe and you shall hear"} {:he "אין בור ירא חטא", :translit "ein bor y'rei cheit", :gloss "an ignoramus is not one who fears sin"} {:he "ולא עם הארץ חסיד", :translit "v'lo am ha'aretz chasid", :gloss "and an am ha'aretz is not pious"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Citing the principle that Torah study is prerequisite to fear of sin and piety."}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Hanina states: 'Anyone who is a Torah scholar, his fear of sin precedes his wisdom' (Shabbat 31a). The same passage warns that an am ha'aretz cannot be a chasid (Shabbat 31a). The idiom 'an ignoramus is not one who fears sin' echoes the Talmudic principle that fear of sin requires learning.", :sources ["Shabbat 31a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כי תעשה הטוב והישר בעיני ה'", :translit "ki ta'aseh ha'tov v'ha'yashar b'Einei HaShem", :gloss "For you shall do the good and the right in the eyes of HaShem"} {:he "כי יכרית", :translit "ki yachrit", :gloss "for he will cut off"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: the phrase about doing what is good and right is adjacent to the phrase about cutting off nations."}], :frame {:text "Moses instructs Israel to 'do what is good and right in the eyes of HaShem' (Deuteronomy 12:28). The next verse begins 'When HaShem your God cuts off the nations' (Deuteronomy 12:29). Rashi on Deuteronomy 12:28 cites the Sifrei connecting 'the good and the right' to acts beyond the strict letter of the law.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 12:28" "Deuteronomy 12:29" "Rashi on Deuteronomy 12:28"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Citing the principle that Torah study is prerequisite to fear of sin and piety.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Semikhah: the phrase about doing what is good and right is adjacent to the phrase about cutting off nations.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:22.284641607Z", :model "glm-5.2"}